  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Between Monaco and Menton, Golfe Bleu beach occupies the Cabbé cove: a pebble beach, with occasionally a few sandy patches, between cliffs and turquoise sea. According to the Menton Riviera &amp; Merveilles tourist office, it is the larger of the cove's two beaches. It is public and supervised in July and August, and also serves as a landing area for paragliders who take off from Mont Gros: if you come with your dog, keep it close when a canopy approaches. Jacques Brel lived in a neighbouring villa and composed several of his songs there.</p>

      <h2>Access on foot</h2>
      <p>The beach can only be reached on foot: either by a flight of stairs from avenue de la Gare (chemin du Golfe Bleu), or by the customs officers' path on the west side, according to the tourist office. The town hall also mentions the Sentier Le Corbusier from the train station. Allow a few minutes' walk with steps to go down, which calls for some care with a large or elderly dog. Access to the beach is free and open all year.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The sources disagree. The Menton Riviera &amp; Merveilles tourist office listing for this beach ticks "animals accepted" without saying where or under what conditions. A Cannes tourist office document (2023) states that dogs are allowed at the eastern end of the commune, on the promenade Robert Schumann, on a leash. Unofficial guides cite a reserved area on the beach, others place it in the west, and a community guide states that the beach no longer accepts dogs since 2025. The town hall's "Les plages" page doesn't mention dogs. No municipal order was found.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: Monaco, right next door, has no beach open to dogs in this guide — the Pointe des Douaniers in Cap-d'Ail or Hawaï beach in Menton are better-documented alternatives.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Menton dog beach is just a few kilometres east, a good option if you're combining several Riviera spots in the same day.</p>
